<p class="fs-4 body-text">
    Hi! Welcome to my portfolio. 
    I'm a software developer with experience building reliable, maintainable software that solves real business problems. 
    My work has focused primarily on C#/.NET and Python, with experience spanning backend development, 
    full-stack applications, automation, data integration, and legacy system modernization.
</p>
<p class="fs-4 body-text">
    My passion for software development started in high school, where I was first introduced to programming through an introductory course. I was immediately hooked and knew early on that this was the career I wanted to pursue.
</p>
<p class="fs-4 body-text">
    My path into software wasn't a straight one. 
    Due to personal circumstances, I spent five years working as a repair technician at Lenovo's repair depot. 
    My time there taught me how to approach problems methodically, troubleshoot under pressure, and focus on finding root causes instead of quick fixes. 
    These are skills I still rely on every day as a software developer.
</p>
<p class="fs-4 body-text">
    Around the time of the pandemic, I decided it was time to fully pursue my passion for software development. 
    I enrolled at Canadore College, completed my diploma with honours, and began my first professional role as a software developer.
</p>
<p class="fs-4 body-text">
    Not long after, I was given the opportunity to continue my education abroad and moved to Ireland to complete my degree at South East Technological University in Carlow. 
    My time at SETU was one of the most formative experiences of my career, where I was exposed to many of the concepts that now define how I approach software development, including clean architecture, SOLID principles, Test Driven Development, secure development, and thoughtful software design.
</p>
<p class="fs-4 body-text">
    After completing my degree, I returned to Canada and joined RBC as a Senior Software Developer. There, I worked on enterprise automation and 
    data integration solutions, modernized legacy processes, supported production systems, and helped improve software quality across 
    multiple codebases.
    That experience reinforced the importance of writing software that is not only functional, but also testable, maintainable, and understandable.
</p>
<p class="fs-4 body-text">
    Today, I continue to build on that foundation through professional development and personal projects, exploring areas such as modern web development, game development, infrastructure, and open-source software. I'm particularly interested in opportunities where I can apply strong engineering fundamentals to challenging problems and continue growing as a developer.
</p>
